cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NNN: a Monte Carlo simulator for rare current events in stochastic lattice models"
message: "If this software supported your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Costa
    given-names: João
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcosta99/monitored-exclusion-rare-events"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A C++20 cloning engine behind a Python interface, estimating the cumulant
  generating function of the time-integrated current in one-dimensional
  exclusion processes, with and without monitoring. It covers the whole
  next-nearest-neighbour rate family, of which WASEP and KLS are the two named
  instances, on an open chain or a periodic ring, through three interchangeable
  event mechanisms. The physics and the population-dynamics algorithm are prior
  work, cited in the accompanying notes; what is offered here is their
  implementation and its validation.
keywords:
  - large deviations
  - cumulant generating function
  - exclusion process
  - population dynamics
  - cloning algorithm
  - Monte Carlo
